  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Kolophon: This book, Pense-Bête, was written by Marcel Broodthaers between 1962-63 and printed in January 1964. Soon after, Broodthaers collaged some of the text with a variety of colored paper. - That spring, he planted the last packaged set (50 copies) of Pense-Bête into plaster, effectuating one of the most pivotal works of his career as a visual artist. - Published as a replica in 2016 by Granary Books in New York City as an edition f 100 numbered copies, modeled on several examples of the collage version with the assistance of Diane Bertolo. Translated into English by Elizabeth Zuba</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Elizabeth Zuba translated the poems into English in collaboration with Maria Gilissen Broodthaers; the edition was produced by Steve Clay and Diane Bertolo, printed by Philip Gallo at The Hermetic Press and bound by Judith Ivry (Quelle: Homepage Granary)</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">In some cases, the paper obstructs part of the poem and in others, one may lift the paper to read the text underneath (Quelle: Homepage Granary)</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Pense-Bête is published on the occasion of "Marcel Broodthaers: A Retrospective" at The Museum of Modern Art, February 14 - May 15, 2016 (Quelle: Homepage Granary)</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The edition comprises 100 copies of which 75 are for sale (Quelle: Homepage Granary)</subfield>
  </datafield>
